      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to use the given information about the arithmetic mean and geometric mean of the real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\).\n\nThe arithmetic mean of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\frac{x + y}{2} = 18\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\\[\nx + y = 36\n\\]\n\nThe geometric mean of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{xy} = \\sqrt{92}\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\nxy = 92\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(x^2 + y^2\\). We can use the identity:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = (x + y)^2 - 2xy\n\\]\nSubstituting the values we have:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = 36^2 - 2 \\cdot 92\n\\]\nCalculating the squares and the product:\n\\[\n36^2 = 1296\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 92 = 184\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = 1296 - 184 = 1112\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(x^2 + y^2\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1112}\n\\]",
